:_:importance:)-6mi9i","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","abstract":[{"text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing: a full-screen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"magenta canvas and a centered white card. The card maps ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Position to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag patch’s logical bounds, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pulses Reset when both position axes are within the placed graph’s 100-point center","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tolerance.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorT